          "In the lower jaw: injury to the nerve that supplies the lip and chin. This is rare and greatly reduced by CBCT planning.",
          "In the upper jaw: proximity to the sinus in the molar region, which is assessed during planning.",
          "Failure of the implant to integrate with the bone (early failure), in which case it is removed and the case reassessed.",
